{{ template "chart.header" . }}

{{ template "chart.badgesSection" . }}

{{ template "chart.description" . }}

This is a **library chart**. It renders nothing on its own: a chart depends on it and calls its
partials to turn a service's configuration into the TOML file and the credential files a
[terrace](https://github.com/TimSchoenle/terrace-config) configuration contract describes. The
`terrace-contract` gates check the rendered result against the image's published contract, so a
chart built on these partials is one they can hold to that contract.

## Usage

```yaml
# Chart.yaml
dependencies:
  - name: terrace-helm
    version: {{ template "chart.version" . }}
    repository: https://timschoenle.github.io/helm-charts
```

```yaml
# templates/configmap.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ `{{ .Release.Name }}` }}
data:
  config.toml: |
    {{ `{{- include "terrace-helm.configToml" (dict "ctx" $ "maps" (list $.Values.config)) | nindent 4 }}` }}
```

```yaml
# templates/deployment.yaml, in the pod spec
{{ `{{- $keys := include "terrace-helm.fileConfig.secretKeys" (dict "ctx" $ "data" .Values.secrets) | fromYamlArray }}` }}
volumes:
  {{ `{{- include "terrace-helm.fileConfig.volumes" (dict "configMapName" .Release.Name "secretName" .Release.Name "secretKeys" $keys) | nindent 2 }}` }}
containers:
  - name: app
    env:
      {{ `{{- include "terrace-helm.fileConfig.env" (dict "ctx" $ "prefix" "MY_APP" "secretKeys" $keys) | nindent 6 }}` }}
    volumeMounts:
      {{ `{{- include "terrace-helm.fileConfig.volumeMounts" (dict "ctx" $ "secretKeys" $keys) | nindent 6 }}` }}
```

Each partial's arguments are documented where it is defined, under `templates/`.

## Partials

| Partial | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `terrace-helm.configToml` | The complete TOML document: merged maps plus the `configExtraToml` escape hatch, refused where the two collide |
| `terrace-helm.tomlMerged` | Deep-merge a list of maps, later entries winning, and render them as TOML |
| `terrace-helm.toml` | Render one map as TOML: tables, scalars, arrays of scalars and arrays of tables |
| `terrace-helm.toml.key`, `.scalar`, `.integer`, `.arrayKind`, `.extraErrors` | The renderer's parts, for a chart that needs one directly |
| `terrace-helm.fileConfig.volumes`, `.volumeMounts` | The config and credential volumes and their read-only mounts |
| `terrace-helm.fileConfig.env` | `<PREFIX>_CONFIG` and `<PREFIX>_SECRETS_DIR`, and nothing else |
| `terrace-helm.fileConfig.secretData`, `.secretKeys`, `.createSecret` | Which credentials a chart's own Secret carries, and whether it renders one |

## Values the partials read

The partials read the consuming chart's values, never values of their own, so the consuming
chart declares and documents these:

| Value | Read by | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `configExtraToml` | `configToml` | Verbatim TOML placed after the rendered top-level keys and before the first table |
| `configMount.configDir` | `fileConfig.volumeMounts`, `fileConfig.env` | Directory the rendered `config.toml` is mounted at |
| `configMount.secretsDir` | `fileConfig.volumeMounts`, `fileConfig.env` | Directory the credential files are mounted at |
| `existingSecret` | `fileConfig.secretKeys`, `fileConfig.createSecret` | An operator-supplied Secret replacing the chart's own |

The ConfigMap and Secret names are arguments, so the consuming chart keeps its own naming.

## Development

The partials are exercised through the `common` library's test fixture,
`.github/testdata/common-fixture`, because `common` depends on this chart and delegates its
`common.toml*`, `common.configToml` and `common.fileConfig.*` names to it.

